    "message": "Show why an intervention preview did not use Opus in the effect explanation\n\nThe Project effect explanation looked for clarification_question and\nexplanation fields that a natural-language CompilerResult never has, and it\ndid not list limitations. The fallback reason added to limitations therefore\nappeared only in the raw JSON under it.\n\nThe panel now says when the result came from the rule path and lists the\nlimitations under a heading that names the reason. The new test runs just\nthat render function in node with stub DOM helpers, fed a real offline\ncompiler result, and skips when node is absent.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
